Say whether a watched KVO key actually changes, cached on the hot path

An application that lays out in a KVO callback is invisible to every other instrument: nothing
draws, nothing raises, and a key that never fires reads as missing layout code. The registration
trace already names who watches what; this names whether the key then changes.

didChangeValueForKey is hot, so the env read is cached in a static rather than scanning environ on
every key change.

Task #194: it measured that iA Writer registers an FBKVO observer on lastKnownCurrentDocument of
IALibraryDocumentController and that key NEVER fires during a row click, so the observer stays
asleep and the editor pane never fills. The trigger that should change it is app code and the seam
is inside the application.
--- a/src/NSKeyValueObserving.m
+++ b/src/NSKeyValueObserving.m
@@ -104,6 +104,20 @@
 
 - (void)didChangeValueForKey:(NSString *)key
 {
+    /* DID THE WATCHED KEY ACTUALLY CHANGE. An application that lays out in a KVO callback needs the
+     * key to fire; a key that never changes leaves the observer asleep and the screen empty with
+     * nothing else to see. Task #194: iA Writer watches lastKnownCurrentDocument and its editor
+     * pane never fills. This runs on EVERY key change, so the env read is cached once rather than
+     * scanning environ per notification. */
+    static int kvoTrace = -1;
+    if (kvoTrace == -1)
+        kvoTrace = (getenv("CIDER_TRACE_KVO") != NULL) ? 1 : 0;
+    if (kvoTrace) {
+        fprintf(stderr, "CIDER_KVO didChange %s of %s\n", [key UTF8String] ?: "(nil)",
+                object_getClassName(self));
+        fflush(stderr);
+    }
+
     pthread_key_t pthreadKVOKey = _NSGetKVOPthreadKey();
     NSKeyValueObservingTSD *kvoTSD = pthread_getspecific(pthreadKVOKey);
     if (kvoTSD != NULL && kvoTSD->pendingNotifications != NULL)
